  data: {
    LLM: "Keep your high-pip tiles for your own arm early in the game. If you have to open your arm, you are inviting others to dump their 9s and 8s on you, making it harder for you to win the round.\n\nOffensive Passing: Sometimes, even if you have a play, it is better to 'Pass' and open your arm if you know your opponent is holding a tile that can only be played on YOUR arm. This traps them into helping you extend your train.\n\nBoneyard Management: In Longana, the boneyard is a resource. If you have only one tile left and it's a double, you might draw from the boneyard intentionally to find a 'blocking' tile to prevent an opponent from going out before you.",
    Player: "Keep your high-pip tiles for your own arm early in the game. If you have to open your arm, you are inviting others to dump their 9s and 8s on you, making it harder for you to win the round.\n\nOffensive Passing: Sometimes, even if you have a play, it is better to 'Pass' and open your arm if you know your opponent is holding a tile that can only be played on YOUR arm. This traps them into helping you extend your train.\n\nBoneyard Management: In Longana, the boneyard is a resource. If you have only one tile left and it's a double, you might draw from the boneyard intentionally to find a 'blocking' tile to prevent an opponent from going out before you.",
